From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Piers Karsenbarg <piers@pulumi.com>
Date: Mon, 20 Jul 2026 09:33:08 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix: aws_rds_cluster storage_type change no longer forces
 replacement

Allow non-Aurora Multi-AZ DB clusters to change storage type in place. Repeat allocation and IOPS when the target storage type requires them, and omit removed IOPS when changing to gp3 below its configurable threshold.

Cover low-storage gp3, reverse gp3-to-io2, unchanged IOPS across provisioned storage types, and explicit gp3 IOPS transitions. The existing gp3 default-IOPS drift remains tracked separately.

Upstream: https://github.com/hashicorp/terraform-provider-aws/pull/48545

diff --git a/.changelog/48545.txt b/.changelog/48545.txt
